{"builder":"Build a new standalone tool, jsonl-lint, as the first workspace under packages/ (packages/ does not exist yet). Plain ES modules, Node 22+, zero runtime dependencies, no build step.\n\n1. Create packages/jsonl-lint/package.json: \"name\": \"jsonl-lint\", \"type\": \"module\", \"scripts\": { \"test\": \"node --test\" }, a \"bin\": { \"jsonl-lint\": \"bin/jsonl-lint.js\" } entry, and no \"dependencies\" (no devDependencies needed either).\n\n2. Create packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js exporting lint(text). Split text on \"\\n\" (strip a trailing \"\\r\" per row). Number rows 1-based by their position in the file. Skip rows that are blank (empty or whitespace only). JSON.parse every other row, including a last row with no trailing newline (an unterminated/torn last row must be checked, not ignored). For each row that fails, push { line, error } where error is the JSON.parse error message string. Return the array (empty when the text is clean). A trailing newline at end of file must not produce a spurious error.\n\n3. Create packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js (shebang #!/usr/bin/env node, executable bit set with git update-index --chmod=+x or chmod +x). Usage: jsonl-lint <file>. With no argument: print a usage message to stderr, exit 2. If the file cannot be read (missing, ENOENT, etc.): print an error to stderr, exit 2. Otherwise run lint on the contents and print one line per error to stdout in the form <file>:<line>: <error> (where <file> is the argument as given), then exit 1 if there were any errors, 0 if none. Use process.exitCode or process.exit after output is written.\n\n4. Create node:test tests under packages/jsonl-lint/test/ (e.g. test/lint.test.js and test/cli.test.js) covering: a clean file (no errors, exit 0); a bad middle row (reports exactly that line number); a torn last row with no trailing newline (reported with its line number); blank lines (skipped, and line numbers of later rows still count the blank lines); and the exit codes of the CLI, run via child_process.spawnSync(process.execPath, [binPath, ...]) against temp files: 0 for clean, 1 for bad rows with the expected <file>:<line>: output, 2 for a missing file, 2 for no argument, each with stderr non-empty for the 2 cases. Make sure `node --test` run inside packages/jsonl-lint finds them (default discovery picks up test/**/*.test.js).\n\n5. Create packages/jsonl-lint/README.md: what it does, usage, output format, exit codes (0/1/2), and the lint(text) API.\n\n6. Update the root README.md: replace the \"No tools yet\" bullet under \"What is here\" with a bullet listing packages/jsonl-lint and a one-line description.\n\n7. Run npm install at the repo root so package-lock.json includes the new workspace (CI runs npm ci, which fails if the lockfile is out of sync). Commit the updated package-lock.json.\n\n8. Run npm ci and npm test at the repo root; both must pass, and npm test must actually run the jsonl-lint tests.\n\n9. Open one pull request on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test whose body contains the line: Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102. Wait for the test workflow (.github/workflows/test.yml) to finish on the PR head and fix anything red until it is green.","verifier":"Check out the PR head. Run every check below at that head, in order, and report PASS or FAIL for each with the evidence (commands and output).\n\nSetup: at the repo root run npm ci. Create temp files in a scratch dir outside the repo, e.g.:\n- clean.jsonl: {\"a\":1}\\n[2]\\n\"x\"\\n\n- badmid.jsonl: {\"a\":1}\\n{bad\\n{\"c\":3}\\n\n- torn.jsonl: {\"a\":1}\\n{\"b\":2}\\n{\"c\": (no trailing newline)\n- blanks.jsonl: {\"a\":1}\\n\\n   \\n{oops\\n\\n (row 4 bad; rows 2, 3, 5 blank)\n\nCheck 1 — expect: \"packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file> prints <file>:<line>: <error> for every row that is not valid JSON (1-based lines, blank lines skipped, an unterminated last line checked) and exits 1 if any, 0 if none\".\nRun node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <path> for each temp file and record stdout and exit status.\nPASS if: clean.jsonl prints no error lines and exits 0; badmid.jsonl prints a line starting with <path>:2: followed by an error text, no line for rows 1 or 3, and exits 1; torn.jsonl prints a line starting with <path>:3: and exits 1; blanks.jsonl prints a line starting with <path>:4: , no lines for blank rows 2, 3 or 5, and exits 1. Also try a file with two bad rows and confirm both are printed.\nFAIL if any of those outputs or exit statuses differ (wrong line number, missing row, blank row reported, torn last row ignored, wrong exit code).\n\nCheck 2 — expect: \"A missing file or no argument prints to stderr and exits 2\".\nRun node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js /nonexistent/x.jsonl, and node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js with no argument, capturing stderr and exit status separately.\nPASS if both exit 2 and both write something non-empty to stderr.\nFAIL if either exits with any other status or writes nothing to stderr.\n\nCheck 3 — expect: \"packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js exports lint(text) returning [{ line, error }]\".\nRun: node --input-type=module -e \"import {lint} from './packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js'; console.log(JSON.stringify(lint('{}\\n{bad\\n')), JSON.stringify(lint('{}\\n')))\" at the repo root.\nPASS if lint is an exported function, the first call returns an array of objects each having a line property (2 for the bad row) and an error property, and the clean call returns an empty array.\nFAIL if the import fails, lint is not exported, or the return shape is not an array of { line, error } objects.\n\nCheck 4 — expect: \"The workspace has its own package.json (jsonl-lint, type module, test script node --test), no runtime dependencies, and node:test tests for a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn last row, blank lines and the exit codes\".\nRead packages/jsonl-lint/package.json and run cd packages/jsonl-lint && npm test. Read the test files.\nPASS if package.json has name jsonl-lint, type module, a test script that runs node --test, no non-empty dependencies field; npm test passes; and the tests (using node:test) cover a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn last row, blank lines, and the CLI exit codes.\nFAIL if any field is wrong or missing, there are runtime dependencies, tests fail, or any of the five listed cases has no test.\n\nCheck 5 — expect: \"packages/jsonl-lint/README.md exists and the root README lists the tool\".\nRun test -f packages/jsonl-lint/README.md and grep -n jsonl-lint README.md.\nPASS if the package README exists and the root README.md mentions jsonl-lint as a tool.\nFAIL if either is missing.\n\nCheck 6 — expect: \"The change is one PR on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test whose body says Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102, and npm test and the test workflow are green at its head\".\nRun gh pr view <pr> --repo suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test --json body,headRefOid,state, gh pr checks <pr> --repo suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test, and npm test at the repo root at the PR head.\nPASS if the change is in a single PR on that repo, its body contains Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102, local npm test passes, and the test workflow run for the head commit is successful.\nFAIL if the body lacks that line, npm test fails, or the test workflow at the head is failing, missing or still pending at the end of your check.\n\nAdvisory (not pass/fail conditions):\n- Confirm npm test at the root actually runs the jsonl-lint tests (look for its test output), and that package-lock.json lists the workspace so npm ci works in CI.\n- Mutation test: in a scratch copy, make lint skip the last row when it has no trailing newline, and confirm the torn-row test fails.\n- Check the bin file has a node shebang and the executable bit, and that CRLF files do not cause spurious errors."}